0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n-3{x}_{2}^{2}\\le 2{x}_{2}^{2},\\,-5{x}_{3}^{2}\\le 2{x}_{3}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-5{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=2(1)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\le 2.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $2.$ But before we conclude that $2$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=2.$\n\nNotice that when $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-5{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2(1)^{2}-3(0)^{2}-5(0)^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378685 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378685 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378685 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378688 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378685 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378685 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186378690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378685 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378685 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378685 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186378686 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378685 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "693f5701-baa5-5230-8d27-8fbfe6ab9c1c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378686 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378686 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378686 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "56933511-7bac-56df-b79c-e43f47de1424" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186378687 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] 